    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Single-Deviation Stability in Additively Separable Hedonic Games with Constrained Coalition Sizes
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Bullinger%2C+M">Martin Bullinger</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Dunajski%2C+A">Adam Dunajski</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Elkind%2C+E">Edith Elkind</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Gilboa%2C+M">Matan Gilboa</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.12641v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        We study stability in additively separable hedonic games when coalition sizes have to respect fixed size bounds. We consider four classic notions of stability based on single-<span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> deviations, namely, Nash stability, individual stability, contractual Nash stability, and contractual individual stability. For each stability notion, we consider two variants: in&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.12641v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.12641v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.12641v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        We study stability in additively separable hedonic games when coalition sizes have to respect fixed size bounds. We consider four classic notions of stability based on single-<span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> deviations, namely, Nash stability, individual stability, contractual Nash stability, and contractual individual stability. For each stability notion, we consider two variants: in one, the coalition left behind by a deviator must still be of a valid size, and in the other there is no such constraint. We provide a full picture of the existence of stable outcomes with respect to given size parameters. Additionally, when there are only upper bounds, we fully characterize the computational complexity of the associated existence problem. In particular, we obtain polynomial-time algorithms for contractual individual stability and contractual Nash stability, where the latter requires an upper bound of 2. We obtain further results for Nash stability and contractual individual stability, when the lower bound is at least 2.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.12641v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.12641v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 14 October, 2025; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2025.
      
    </p>
    

    

    
